# tracks_px.scene.jsonl - a longer pixel-space scene, 33 s, 12 tracks.\n\nSame camera as tracks_px.sample.jsonl. Tracks 1-4 are that fixture; tracks\n5-12 add four more crossing conflicts in two later acts, separated in time\nand space so no pair interacts across acts:\n\n  5+6    car x auto         min TTC 0.70 s\n  7+8    truck x motorcycle min TTC 1.10 s\n  9+10   bus x car          min TTC 0.55 s\n  11+12  motorcycle x car   min TTC 0.95 s\n\nIn each pair the second vehicle BRAKES as it reaches the crossing. That is\nwhat makes these near-misses rather than collisions: two vehicles held at\nconstant velocity on a converging course simply overlap, and the engine\nthen correctly but uselessly reports TTC = 0. Someone reacting is what\nproduces a real minimum TTC, and it is what happens on real footage.\n\nEach conflict is specified by the MINIMUM TTC it should produce rather than\nby a magic timestamp, so the severity that comes out can be justified.\n\nThis file is the source of fixtures/events.edge.sample.json, which is what\nowners D, E and F code against from hour 2.
